A||||6||redfiero||My car died today!||||8||
Z||000000||redfiero||09-27-2001||11:13 AM||||On the way to work today, driving along like usual and the car dies.  Flat out turns off!  Radio works, lights work, car turns over, just won't start.  Pulled a plug wire and doesn't look like I'm getting any spark.  My guess is that its something in the ignition.  Probably the coil packs??  Anyone have any ideas?  Its an 88 4 cylinder.<P>Thanks,<BR>matt||||reg||8
Z||000001||Kasdan||09-27-2001||12:07 PM||||Check out the ignition switch and the coil, those would by my guess.  If its an MSD coil..well, we all know about those.<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero21.jpg">         <BR>Power Steering, Holley Scoop<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
Z||000002||Hank is Here||09-27-2001||12:36 PM||||I doubt that it is the coils.   There are four seperate coils in two packs and the chance of all four gonig out at exactly the same time is practically non-existant||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||09-27-2001||01:14 PM||||There's a module associated with the coils. Check "Ogre's Cave" link at the top of the page. When you get there, look for "DIS notes".<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 09-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||redfiero||09-28-2001||06:15 AM||||Thanks for the suggestions.  I will be (hopefully) fixing it tomorrow!<P>matt||||reg||7
Z||000005||theogre||09-28-2001||08:36 PM||||Be extremely carfull with DIS motors. That ignition has over twice the power of an HEI system.<P>It just shut off? If you still have spark, check both coils, I doubt it's ignition. Check for fuel problems.<P>When testing spark on a DIS motor you really want one of those spark testers with the adjustable gap that you can get at allot of parts stores.... Getting bit by coils can be fatal. DIS coils are worse...<P>No fuel could be:<BR>1. bad pump<BR>2. bad regulator or regulator jammed open.<BR>3. bad wire<BR>4. bad injector <BR>5. bad ecm<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||09-28-2001||08:41 PM||||Almost forgot.... check the thin wires off the battery and the ground straps bolted all over the block and bell housing. Any of those could also cause it to shut off. <P>You'll have to disasseble and inspect all of them. corrosion may not kill it conpletetly but can make it so weak it has the same effect.||||reg||1
